    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d198">

                <pb facs="0375" n="335" sameAs="frus:frus1865p1/pg335"/>

                <head>Mr. Hunter to Mr.
                        Adams</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1384.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-05-02"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 2, 1865</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your despatch of the 30th of March, No.
                    914, together with its accompanying copy of a series of resolutions adopted at a
                    meeting in London, expressive of a desire to aid the Freedmen’s Relief
                    Association in the accomplishment of their object has been received. The great
                    calamity which befell the nation previous to the arrival of your communication
                    deprived the association of the countenance and encouragement of the late
                    distinguished President, to whom it was the intention of the meeting that these
                    resolutions should have been presented. You may thank them in the behalf of the
                    present Chief Magistrate for their kindly sympathy with so worthy a cause, and
                    inform them that a copy of their resolutions will be laid before that
                    association.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. HUNTER, <hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                    Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
